  "nutritionSource": "USDA FoodData Central: SR Legacy (pork, flour, canola, cabbage, onion, eggs, scallion, sugar) and Branded Foods labels (Nishiki, Kikkoman soy and panko, Hondashi, Morton). Batter, panko and oil counted at the amounts MEXT measured on fried pork loin (Japan Food Composition Tables 2020, table 13: per 100 g raw pork, 3.7 g flour, 9.3 g panko, 13.4 g oil absorbed). Water and pepper not counted.",
  "swaps": null,
  "notes": [
    "No mirin or sake. Each tbsp of mirin is replaced with 2 tsp sugar plus 1 tbsp water, which matches mirin’s ≈49% sugar.",
    "Flour-and-water batter instead of egg wash keeps every egg for the bowl, and it’s the method MEXT measured. Mitsuba is the traditional garnish if you can find it.",
    "Katsudon is the classic use for leftover tonkatsu, since the crust softens in the sauce anyway."
